.TH CLIPNEST-CTL 1 "2026" "clipnest" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipnest-ctl \- control a running Clipnest instance over D-Bus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipnest-ctl
\fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipnest-ctl
is a thin wrapper around Clipnest's D-Bus service
.RI ( app.clipnest.Clipnest ,
activated automatically if not already running \- see
.IR /usr/share/dbus-1/services/app.clipnest.Clipnest.service ).
It never talks to the network and never spawns Clipnest itself; D-Bus
activation handles that.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B toggle-picker
Open or close the clipboard-history picker. Runs
.B clipnest \-\-toggle\-picker
directly (which forwards to an already-running instance, or starts one).
.TP
.B expand-snippet
Expand the current text selection as a snippet keyword. Runs
.B clipnest \-\-expand\-snippet
directly, same as
.BR toggle-picker .
.TP
.B open-settings
Open Clipnest's Settings window. Calls the running instance's D-Bus
control interface directly (D-Bus-activating it first if it isn't
already running).
.TP
.B ping
Check that Clipnest is running and responding. Also D-Bus-activates it
if it isn't already running.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed
.B clipnest
version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clipnest (1)
